   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Microphones have replaced radar images and morning counts as the only reliable way to study bird migration.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Certain warblers pass over Harrowgate in large numbers on nights when almost none are seen the next morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Recording night flight calls reveals migrating birds that morning counts miss, and despite its limits the method helps a town understand and protect them.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Migrating songbirds call at night mainly to warn one another about tall buildings and bright lights.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Recording night flight calls reveals migrating birds that morning counts miss, and despite its limits the method helps a town understand and protect them.$q$, $q$The passage explains the problem with morning counts, how listening solves it, the method's limits and its use in protecting birds, so the second choice covers the whole text. The warbler finding is only one piece of evidence from paragraph 3.$q$, 'draft', 'd7e45505-307c-5593-ba89-29005b3e5902')
