   $q$How do the findings from Harrowgate develop the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They prove that cold fronts are the main cause of songbird migration each autumn.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"They explain why migrating birds give short, high calls while flying in the dark.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"They show that the microphones recorded fewer species than researchers had hoped to find.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They give concrete evidence that listening detects birds that morning counts miss, such as warblers seen rarely by day.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They give concrete evidence that listening detects birds that morning counts miss, such as warblers seen rarely by day.$q$, $q$The warblers that "passed over in large numbers on nights when almost none were seen the next morning" show exactly what listening adds. The passage says north winds "helped the birds along," not that cold fronts cause migration.$q$, 'draft', 'd7e45505-307c-5593-ba89-29005b3e5902')
