  ('192e12a4-9d59-5647-9bac-0de04d0ada20', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"An archive's wax cylinders are too fragile to play, so it photographs their grooves and uses software to calculate the sound. The method is slow and needs human checking, but it has recovered recordings unheard for a century.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Wax cylinders were made by cutting a groove with a needle. The Calloway archive holds about two thousand of them, and many are cracked, moldy or brittle after a hundred years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Wax cylinders hold songs and speeches from a century ago. The archive's wonderful new method is the most exciting thing to happen in sound history, and every listener will be moved by the lullaby.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"An archive in Calloway uses cameras and software to perfectly restore every wax cylinder in its collection. Because the method is automatic, the archive no longer needs people to check the recordings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An archive's wax cylinders are too fragile to play, so it photographs their grooves and uses software to calculate the sound. The method is slow and needs human checking, but it has recovered recordings unheard for a century.$q$, $q$The third choice covers the problem, the method, its limits and its results without adding opinions. The first choice sounds neutral but contradicts paragraph 4, which describes hiss and a team that listens to every file.$q$, 'draft', '5c88cc63-fe99-595e-9c39-ef5b5a213fd2')
