   $q$Which statement best expresses the central idea of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Modern lane lines are strings of plastic discs that spin when water hits them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Pool features that reduce waves help make races fairer, so results depend more on swimmers than on their lanes.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Swimmers in the outside lanes usually lose races because they are less skilled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Deep pools turn slow swimmers into fast ones by removing the force of the water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Pool features that reduce waves help make races fairer, so results depend more on swimmers than on their lanes.$q$, $q$The passage explains several wave-reducing features and ends by saying they make results depend "more on the swimmers than on the lane." The spinning discs are one supporting detail, and the passage says nothing makes a slow swimmer fast.$q$, 'draft', '79e6575b-848f-55d7-8f2a-eb00e44be484')
