  ('40541be4-f679-5811-8efa-76dd115fd32f', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g10-main-idea-summary'), null, 'hard',
   $q$How does the final paragraph refine the central idea?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It admits that the rule of doing less is mostly an excuse for avoiding difficult repairs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It introduces a new rule that conservators should follow when the first rule fails.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It corrects a likely misunderstanding, showing that doing less still demands skill because the aim is preservation, not renewal.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It suggests that conservators should return to reweaving once they have done enough research.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It corrects a likely misunderstanding, showing that doing less still demands skill because the aim is preservation, not renewal.$q$, $q$The paragraph raises the idea that the rule "can seem like doing nothing" and then answers it: the work "demands patience, careful research and great skill." The first choice takes the misunderstanding as the writer's point.$q$, 'draft', 'f0f47798-5f61-5692-b34e-a0cf519c10fe')
