   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"At Calder General, each wing now has a color and a plain name. Floor stripes lead from the main entrance, and elevator lobbies display maps with a bold marker showing where visitors are standing.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Calder General's staff refused to give visitors directions, so the hospital built new wings with clearer hallways. After the building was finished, fewer visitors were late for appointments.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"distorts-text"},{"text":"Hospitals are confusing and stressful places. Calder General's brilliant design team solved every problem, and all hospitals should hire them to fix their hallways right away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Many Calder General visitors needed directions, taking staff from patient care. A design team watched visitors, found confusing terms and numbers, and added plain names, colors, floor stripes, maps and clearer letters. Requests for directions then dropped sharply.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many Calder General visitors needed directions, taking staff from patient care. A design team watched visitors, found confusing terms and numbers, and added plain names, colors, floor stripes, maps and clearer letters. Requests for directions then dropped sharply.$q$, $q$The second choice includes the problem, the research, the changes and the result without judgment. The third choice is accurate but leaves out the problem and the outcome.$q$, 'draft', '2123051e-13ae-5606-908b-acb521fc62b7')
