   $q$What is the writer's central claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Worksheets, screens and videos have no value in a high school science class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Westbrook High should spend most of its science time outdoors instead of preparing for tests.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"},{"text":"Imani Castellanos discovered why one side of a maple tree leafs out later.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Science students should keep weekly outdoor field notebooks because they build the careful observation that science depends on.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Science students should keep weekly outdoor field notebooks because they build the careful observation that science depends on.$q$, $q$The writer states the claim at the end of paragraph 1 and gives careful observation as "the strongest reason." The writer says screens and worksheets have value, and Imani designed an experiment but the passage does not say she found the answer.$q$, 'draft', '09532bbe-2025-5fbf-af6d-ed587b3fd74f')
