   $q$Which is the most objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The writer describes a field notebook. Students pick a spot such as a tree or a lawn, return to it regularly, sketch what they see, note the weather and write questions over many months.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Field notebooks are the best way to teach science. Weekly sketching makes students observe carefully, as Imani's maple tree shows, and teachers who worry about tests are simply wrong.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"presents-opinion-as-fact"},{"text":"The writer convincingly proves that field notebooks are better than screens. With a brilliant example and a strong reply to critics, the piece should persuade every science teacher at Westbrook.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"The writer argues that science students should keep weekly outdoor field notebooks, mainly because sketching teaches careful observation, as in a student's maple tree study. The writer answers concerns about test time and says notebooks would add to screens, not replace them.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The writer argues that science students should keep weekly outdoor field notebooks, mainly because sketching teaches careful observation, as in a student's maple tree study. The writer answers concerns about test time and says notebooks would add to screens, not replace them.$q$, $q$An objective summary of an opinion piece reports the writer's claim and reasons without adopting or judging them, which the third choice does. The first choice states the writer's opinion as fact and adds a judgment the writer did not make, since the writer called the concern "fair."$q$, 'draft', '09532bbe-2025-5fbf-af6d-ed587b3fd74f')
